1️⃣ Purpose of python manage.py migrate
In Django, the migrate command is used to:
Apply database migrations.
Create the tables and schema in your database that correspond to your Django models.
Keep the database schema in sync with your code.
  Essentially, it sets up your database according to your app’s models.Running python manage.py migrate tells Python to execute the manage.py script and apply all pending migrations.

